This distribution is built on Electron (MIT License), which contains
Chromium, Node.js and V8 under their own licenses. It also embeds
third-party fonts and data files from `typst-assets` (Apache License,
Version 2.0), which the Typst compiler used by the PDF renderer
(desktop/pdf.ts, via @myriaddreamin/typst-ts-node-compiler) carries in
its native addon to typeset invoices without relying on fonts installed
on the user's system — most notably Libertinus Serif (SIL Open Font
License), which is what lets invoices render Czech diacritics correctly.
The full text of that Apache License, the attribution notices for every
bundled font and data file, and the list of npm packages shipped in the
application are reproduced, as required, in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
